  "root_problem": "CRM dispute volume sustained a ~2x increase from a ~600/month baseline (Jun-Jul 2026) to 1180-1260/month in Aug-Sep 2026 (E-06). Of the 1,240 ESTIMATED-read disputed bills (41% of 3,025 disputed bills, E-02), 1,184 (95.5%) trace to billing-import rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01, rejecting valid AMI reads as REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION (E-12) because BV-17 compares raw register values with no unit scaling (E-13) against meters on v4.2 firmware, which records readings in 0.1 m3 units instead of the plain m3 units v3.x firmware uses (E-14) - a mismatch that makes normal consumption appear ~10x higher than the 12-month m3 history BV-17 checks against. This BV-17 unit-scaling defect is the best-evidenced mechanism for the ESTIMATED-read dispute pathway; whether it also explains the larger ACTUAL-read disputed-bill share (59%, 1,785/3,025, E-02) is untested and tracked separately."
 },
